# 5. Paid end-to-end monitoring services

Yes. There is an entire industry around this.

A few major options are:

| Platform | Main strength | PayslipMax |
|---|---|---|
| Firebase Crashlytics | Excellent crash reporting | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ |
| [Sentry](https://sentry.io?utm_source=chatgpt.com) | Errors + performance + tracing | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ |
| [Embrace](https://embrace.io?utm_source=chatgpt.com) | Mobile-first observability | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ |
| [Bugsnag](https://www.bugsnag.com?utm_source=chatgpt.com) | App stability/release health | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ |
| [Datadog](https://www.datadoghq.com?utm_source=chatgpt.com) | Full enterprise observability | ⭐⭐⭐ |
| [New Relic](https://newrelic.com?utm_source=chatgpt.com) | Enterprise APM/observability | ⭐⭐⭐ |

Bugsnag, for example, automatically captures uncaught Java/Kotlin exceptions, native crashes and ANRs and tracks sessions to calculate release stability.  Embrace goes considerably deeper into mobile-specific diagnostics, including ANR monitoring. 

But **I wouldn't pay for these yet**.

You have roughly four testers.

Your initial stack should be:

**Crashlytics + Play Console + good instrumentation + automated testing.**

At thousands/tens of thousands of active users, revisit Sentry/Embrace/Datadog depending on your needs.

