# 6. There's another tool you should start using immediately

## Google Play Pre-launch Report

This is extremely valuable for an indie developer.

Before production, Google can automatically run your application on various devices and identify issues.

Play Console crash reports can also link issues discovered during pre-launch testing with device information, logs and video. 

Think of it as Google lending you a cupboard full of Android phones.

So your testing becomes:

```text
YOUR PHONE
      +
EMULATORS
      +
CLOSED TESTERS
      +
GOOGLE PRE-LAUNCH TEST DEVICES
```

Much better than testing only on your own Android device.

---

# 7. Release builds must be tested — not merely debug builds

This is **very important**.

A classic beginner mistake is:

```text
Android Studio Debug build

✓ Everything works

            ↓

Play Store Release build

💥 crashes
```

Release builds can behave differently because of:

- R8
- ProGuard
- minification
- resource shrinking
- signing
- different API keys
- different Firebase configuration
- different environment variables
- release-only optimisations
- permissions
- RevenueCat/store billing
- backend restrictions

Therefore:

> **The actual release build is a separate test target.**

For every release, test the release variant.

---

# 8. Symbolication/de-obfuscation is essential

Suppose Crashlytics reports:

```text
a.b.c.a(SourceFile:17)
```

Almost useless.

You want:

```text
GrammarAwareParser.parseGrid()
GrammarAwareParser.kt:184
```

If R8/ProGuard obfuscation is enabled, your mapping files must reach Crashlytics.

Otherwise you might finally receive your crash report and discover that you still can't understand it.

---

# 9. Set up alerts

You shouldn't have to keep opening Firebase every morning.

Crashlytics can alert on new issues, regressions and issues whose occurrence is increasing. 

Eventually, your workflow should be:

```text
                 USER
                   │
                CRASH
                   │
                   ▼
              Crashlytics
                   │
        ┌──────────┴─────────┐
        ▼                    ▼
Crash grouped           Alert generated
with similar crashes          │
        │                     ▼
        └──────────────→ YOU
                              │
                              ▼
                         investigate
                              │
                              ▼
                             fix
                              │
                              ▼
                          v1.0.4
```

You shouldn't depend on:

> Tester → WhatsApp → "Sir app crashed."

