# 17. Your test data corpus is particularly important

PayslipMax isn't a generic app.

Its core risk is:

> **PDF → extraction → classification → parsing → financial representation**

You already have payslips across multiple PCDA formats.

Turn those into a permanent regression corpus.

Something like:

```text
/tests/payslips/

2019/
2020/
2021/
2022/
2023/
2024/
2025/
2026/

ExpectedResults/
```

Every release should automatically run the parser against the corpus.

If:

```text
Previous release
48/48 PASS

New release
45/48 PASS
```

the pipeline should fail.

**Don't ship.**

This is arguably more valuable to PayslipMax than buying Datadog.

