# 19. Monitor performance, not just crashes

A user saying:

> "PayslipMax crashed."

could actually mean:

> "I tapped import and nothing happened for 15 seconds, so I closed it."

That's potentially an **ANR/performance issue**, not a crash.

Track things such as:

```text
App cold start
PDF opening
PDF extraction
Parsing duration
Database loading
Archive loading
Backup
AI report generation
```

Example:

```text
PDF extraction       380 ms
Parser               140 ms
Database write        22 ms

Total                542 ms
```

versus:

```text
PDF extraction       900 ms
Parser             12,400 ms   ← problem
Database write        40 ms
```

Observability tells you something is slow before it necessarily crashes.

---

# 20. Don't log everything

This is another beginner trap.

You don't want:

```text
10,000 lines of random logs
```

You want **structured events at important boundaries**.

For example:

```text
IMPORT_STARTED

PDF_OPEN_SUCCESS
PDF_OPEN_FAILED

FORMAT_DETECTED

PARSER_STARTED
PARSER_SUCCESS
PARSER_FAILED

VALIDATION_SUCCESS
VALIDATION_FAILED

DB_WRITE_STARTED
DB_WRITE_SUCCESS
DB_WRITE_FAILED
```

That creates a comprehensible story.

